{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/769625-game-breaking-how-to-house-rule","id":769625,"title":"Game Breaking: How to House Rule?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-19T16:35:05-08:00","id":769625,"title":"Game Breaking: How to House Rule?","content":"So It's been brought to my attention that the Epic Attributes can get pretty damn crazy down the line when the Automatic Successes come into play. I have been warned that once you get to Demigod level, anything with more Epic Dexterity than you is pretty much guaranteed to win a fight every time. In order to overcome this, people tend to use house rules and home brewed methods, but I don't know of any examples to help balance the game out.<br /> <br /> <br /> One possible idea I had was to simply downgrade them to 1 auto success per level (12 successes at max), but I don't know if this would dramatically reduce the effectiveness of these attributes from a story telling point. Say if a building needed 60 successes to lift and you only have a dice pool of 20 with 12 automatic successes. Technically your character might be able to lift the weight of the building, but mechanically it would be impossible to roll the successes needed to actually do it.<br /> <br /> So could anybody help me out with making the game more properly balanced so I don't have a horde of dex monkies running around smacking people into the dirt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T17:06:39-08:00","id":769649,"title":"","content":"I'd decouple how much you can lift from how many successes you need to lift it \u2014 that is, the more dots of Epic Strength you have, the more mass each success lets you lift. More generally, keep it to one success per level, but scale what that one success means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T17:34:57-08:00","id":769666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/769625-game-breaking-how-to-house-rule?p=769649#post769649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd decouple how much you can lift from how many successes you need to lift it \u2014 that is, the more dots of Epic Strength you have, the more mass each success lets you lift. More generally, keep it to one success per level, but scale what that one success means.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm a bit confused as to what you mean, if you could please clarify?<br /> <br /> It sounds like you're suggesting making the Epics subtract from the successes needed for the roll. But I'm still confused how this would apply to character vs character actions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T19:25:58-08:00","id":769722,"title":"","content":"Just wondering... I know people mention that the super high DV values sort of break things at higher levels but I noticed something the other day when a player of mine was creating his character. Why don't people just use followers against these single super fast targets? They are easily available, in bulk, and with the 1 dot birthright choice for having them respawn on their own is readily available within the companion book. Now sure, I'd atleast require a day or so to pass before they did respawn but certainly that is a easy counter to this type of enemy. A player in my group has a group of 15 archers (cops reskinned) ready to be summoned and spam attack a single target to drop their DV 1 per attack as per the normal rules. Id assume like most RPGs you are capable of attacking with followers (summons) the moment they appear.<br /> <br /> Sooo yea... just a suggestion.<br /> <br /> Oh yea, I also nerfed unavoidable opponent to +1 DV per dot in epic dex instead of doubling it. That also seemed to be a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T19:32:36-08:00","id":769726,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately I don't have Companion yet. Planning to get God and Companion for Christmas, and still undecided on whether or not to get Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> <br /> The thing is though, epic attributes add automatic successes, the number of which doubles with each level. At 10 Epic Dex, you get 44 automatic successes on top of whatever you roll normally. Which is why it's considered to be game breaking for people when a character just auto dodges everything around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-19-2015, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T19:43:18-08:00","id":769730,"title":"","content":"True, but if you are relatively close to their dex level (2 or 3 lower) then a solid group of fodder could assist. Although thinking about it... I think I also remember a rule saying a character could choose to directly take a hit without dodging it. I guess if a threat was smart enough they would know their soak would cover each projectile and just simply not try and dodge. I just think its the DM's job to make sure they don't send enemies at their players that tower over them in epic dex levels. I've just learned to embrace epic attributes as a &quot;you get what you ask for&quot; system. Want to be accurate in battle? Take Epic Dex. Want dmg? Take Epic Strength. Sure, it kinda sucks that everyone is drawn into taking epic dex but if your DM also understands that he could always toss out more XP as well so dabbling into it doesn't cripple you from investing into other things. The biggest benefit of this game is how easily mod-able it is even on the fly. Very flexible and adaptable system.<br /> <br /> This may not help you with your issue, but randomly decided to post. Ignore if you wish, sorry!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T20:05:31-08:00","id":769734,"title":"","content":"Because Followers almost never have Epic Attributes. They become almost entirely useless after Legend 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T23:01:00-08:00","id":769788,"title":"","content":"Actually, it seems like the most a follower can get is 4 levels of epic attribute, which is child's to somebody with 12 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T06:44:50-08:00","id":769939,"title":"","content":"When Dataweaver was suggesting decoupling the amount one can lift from the number of successes needed to lift it, I believe he was more or less suggesting that one shouldn't need to roll to see if one can lift something, rather calculate the amount they can lift based on their Strength+Athletics and level of Epic Strength and Knacks. Now, with a mundane Strength of 10 and Athletics 5, one should be able to lift roughly 2200 pounds (over a ton). Epic Strength 10 adds 1,250,000,000 pounds to this total (625,000 tons), while the Uplifting Might Knack doubles this (1,250,002 tons).<br /> <br /> So, if the object is within this weight capacity (and at over a million tons, there would be very little that isn't in this capacity), he should be able to lift it without too much trouble.<br /> <br /> Now as a Feat of Strength that would require a roll, I would allow such an epically strong character to lift a capacity of his maximum strength times the number of successes he rolls, so with an Epic Strength of 10, even limiting them to 10 automatics successes, that is a minimum of 10 times this amount (over 12 million tons); not including any successes they get from rolling their base dice pool of 15 dice (for an average of another 5 successes, with a maximum potential for 30 more... if all the dice roll 10). Thus, a God at this level would have a maximum potential of around 50 million tons (give or take a couple of million) of lifting capacity as a feat of strength. Can you think of anything that would exceed this weight limit that a God might want to move (other than celestial objects like moons, planets and such)?<br /> <br /> And that is without using the Ultimate Expression of Strength.<br /> <br /> And just to be clear... there is no Strength 12 and such... all Attributes go from 1 to 10, including Epics. Only Legend goes higher because one needs a higher Legend than their highest attribute (you need Legend 11 to reach Attribute and Epic 10 and Legend 12 to get Ultimate Expressions of an Attribute or a Purview Avatar) and Ultimate Expressions are not exactly equal to an 11th dot (they are the ultimate expression of an Attribute and as such do not abide by an conceivable limitations to that attribute. With Ultimate Strength, there is nothing in the Universe that the character can not lift (without ever needing to make any kind of roll).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":2243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","user":"Shadowstripe","date":". 11-20-2015, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T17:11:06-08:00","id":770389,"title":"","content":"What I was suggesting is to use your Attribute roll as normal (including the one autosuccess per dot of Epic), but to change what the resulting successes <i>mean</i> based on how many dots of Epic you have. <br /> <br /> As the rules are written, each success always gives you 25 lbs of lifting capacity, and that gets supplemented by a fixed amount that your Epic Strength provides: 500 lbs for Epic \u2022, 1000 lbs for Epic \u2022\u2022, and so on. The only reason those initial 25 lbs per success mean anything at all is that you get a boatload of successes to work with: the official progression of auto-successes converges on a doubling of how many you are given with each dot, so Epic \u2022\u2022\u2022 not only gives you 2000 lbs of lifting capacity outright, it also gives you 7 successes-worth of lifting capacity on top of that, or an additional 175 lbs. Add to that another 25 lbs per success that you actually roll. Note that the auto-successes don't quite reach a tenth of what Epic Strength grants you outright. <br /> <br /> After a while, it becomes pointless to roll Strength + Athletics to lift something, because 25 lbs per success rolled is inconsequential compared to the tons worth of lifting capacity granted by the Epic. Dropping things to one auto-success per dot of Epic actually doesn't affect things all that much, as the amount of lifting capacity granted by the auto-successes as written never breaks even a tenth of what the Epic grants on its own. <br /> <br /> So, back to my suggestion: instead of each success granting 25 lbs, say that how much each success grants you depends on your Epic. Instead of a flat +500 lbs from Epic \u2022, say that at Epic \u2022 every success that you get on the roll lets you lift 250 lbs; Epic \u2022\u2022 grants +500 lbs per success instead of a flat +1000 lbs; Epic \u2022\u2022\u2022 grants +1000 lbs per success instead of a flat +2000 lbs; and so on. Now your dice pool actually matters. <br /> <br /> The other thing a linear progression of auto-successes does is to drastically scale back how much damage you can inflict. Three options here: stick to the existing system (meaning that if your Epic Strength exceeds your opponent's Epic Stamina by one at the high end, he's dead meat if you hit him); go with a linear progression (meaning that you won't be able to rip tanks in half); or go with a hybrid approach where you use a linear progression of one auto-success against significant opponents such as other Scions, but you use the published escalation of auto-successes when you're chewing the scenery. The last approach isn't particularly realistic; but it lets you be awesome without making a single dot's difference in Epic ratings literally a matter of life or death. <br /> <br /> A fourth possibility would be to downgrade the armor ratings of tanks and the like. <br /> <br /> For Epic Dexterity, keep the boost to Move and Dash as is, but reduce the DV bonus to a linear progression of one per dot of Epic. The wonkiness of the current system lies entirely in the geometric progression of DV and auto-successes, meaning that as you get higher in the scale a single dot of Epic Dex more than your opponent has means that he'll never be able to generate enough successes to hit you and you will always have enough successes to hit him; linearize those progressions, and the problem goes away. <br /> <br /> The advice I gave for damage-dealing Epic Strength also applies to damage-soaking Epic Stamina. <br /> <br /> Social and Mental Epics need no further tampering beyond putting their auto-successes on a linearity diet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T17:54:28-08:00","id":770413,"title":"","content":"Ah, well on the subject of weight limit to auto success, I was actually using that an example. The major problem I'm having it trying to figure out how to balance out Epic Dexterity, since it doesn't matter how much you can lift or how much pain you can tolerate if you've got some anime character warping in and out of combat, decapitating 30 people in one action.<br /> <br /> But yeah, my initial idea for the epics was something along that line of the Superman approach where the characters utilize the attribute as they need it. Meaning a character could possibly lift 500 tons over their head, but that doesn't mean they're going to be punching everybody into space every time they enter battle.<br /> <br /> In other words, reduce / remove the auto success but keep the rest of the Epic benefits such as increase move / weight limit / endurance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T08:08:54-08:00","id":770737,"title":"","content":"One thing on the terms of houserules. many add perception and epic perceptoin to the damage of ranged attacks as far as I'm aware<br /> <br /> else downgrading to 1 automatic success per epic dot is what I do myself in every game (same for untouchable opponent)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}